    pr_ref:  # bf42
    description: "Per the WI-dumiz-bikul audit verdict (DEPRECATE — full ADR-0023-shape migration), draft ADR-0027 instantiating ADR-0024's four-part axis-declaration template for Symbol.kind. The audit's cluster taxonomy (in WI-dumiz-bikul's discussion thread) is the input to §1 Context and §3 Detailed analysis.\n\nADR-0027 SCOPE:\n- §1 Context: 192 distinct values across 8+ axes; reference the audit verdict.\n- §2 Decision: Symbol.kind names the SOURCE-LANGUAGE SYNTACTIC CONSTRUCT only. Cluster A from the audit (~30 values: function, class, method, struct, ...) is the canonical seed; framework participation moves to meta keys; edge labels reclassify or move.\n- §3 Detailed analysis: per-cluster fold targets (cluster D → kind=function/method + meta['framework_role']='event_publisher' etc.; cluster E → reclassify as call_site / drop; cluster F overlaps with ADR-0023's component value; cluster G arguably a separate axis).\n- §4 Consumer pattern: consumers query (kind, edge_type, meta) per ADR-0023 §6 Phase 2 shape.\n- §5 Enforcement: axis_drift.find_drift parameterized on name_filter='SYMBOL_KIND' with the new registry; per-axis property test; pre-commit linter via scripts/check-symbol-kind-drift (analogous to check-edge-type-drift).\n- §6 Migration plan: four phases mirroring ADR-0023 §6 (registry + linter, consumer migration, producer migration, schema bump + removal).\n\nESTIMATED EFFORT: ADR-0027 draft itself: ~1 day for the writing. Migration phases: cumulatively ~5-10 days, plus bakeoff validation per phase.\n\nFOLLOW-UP ITEMS: After ADR-0027 lands, file separate items for each phase (registry, drift linter, consumer migration, producer migration, schema bump) — same pattern as the WI-sahab-fatoz / WI-mokam-jalig / WI-vomoj-suhaz chain for ADR-0023.\n\nDEPENDENCIES: none HARD; SOFT dependency on ADR-0024 (axis-declaration template — already accepted, used as the authoritative format)."  # bf42
    fields: {}  # bf42
- op: discuss  # 46ad
  at: '2026-05-02T04:55:25Z'  # 46ad
  by: agent  # 46ad
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 46ad
  clock: 2  # 46ad
  nonce: 46ad  # 46ad
  message: "**Audit-findings filing convention** (added 2026-05-02 in light of WI-rodub PR #3507).\n\nPer-cluster fold-target verdicts that emerge during ADR-0027 drafting OR during Phase 3 producer migration file as audit-findings documents at `docs/audits/<NN>-<topic>.md` (format spec: `docs/audits/README.md`; verdict methodology: ADR-0024 §\"Family-audit verdict methodology\"), **NOT** as a new ADR and **NOT** as embedded verdict tables in ADR-0027 itself.\n\nThe split:\n\n- **High-level cluster taxonomy** (cluster A canonical seed, cluster D folds to `function/method` + `meta['framework_role']='event_publisher'`, cluster E reclassifies as `call_site` / drop, cluster F overlaps with ADR-0023's `component` value, cluster G arguably a separate axis) **stays in ADR-0027 §3**. This is the equivalent of ADR-0023's §6 high-level deprecation list.\n\n- **Per-value CANONICAL / FOLD / DEPRECATE-NO-FOLD verdicts** with structured `diagnostic_test` (cmd + expect) and `rationale` per row go into the audit-findings doc(s). Likely shape: one audit-findings doc per cluster (e.g., `docs/audits/0003-symbol-kind-cluster-d-framework-roles.md`), or one umbrella doc per audit pass — author's judgment, mirroring how audit-findings 0001 covered both the dispatch and publish families together because they share methodology.\n\nWorked examples of the audit-findings format:\n- `docs/audits/0001-dispatch-publish-family.md` (originally ADR-0025; 13 rows across two families)\n- `docs/audits/0002-ipc-family.md` (originally ADR-0026; 7 rows)\n\nMechanical-check predicates per row's status (UNRESOLVED / PRELIM_RESOLVED / RESOLVED) are validated by `packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_audit_findings.py` and the `scripts/check-audit-findings` pre-commit gate. Both consume `hypergumbo_core.audit_findings`. When ADR-0027 lands, the registry mapping in `audit_findings._REGISTRIES` will need extending: add `\"Symbol.kind\": SYMBOL_KINDS` (or whatever the registry tuple is named) so the property test can validate Symbol.kind-axis audit-findings docs against the live registry. The mechanical-check predicates (RESOLVED + CANONICAL → present on canonical section; RESOLVED + FOLD/DEPRECATE-NO-FOLD → absent; PRELIM_RESOLVED → present on deprecation-candidate section; UNRESOLVED → present any axis) are already defined generically in `validate_against_registry` and don't need re-implementing — they read the spec's axis from the registry tuple.\n\nThis convention prevents re-creating the structural confusion that produced ADR-0025/0026 (per-value verdict tables filed as ADRs in error). The bucket boundary is documented in `docs/adr/README.md`."  # 46ad
